            "Benito"
          ],
          "members": [],
          "is_group": false,
          "biography": "Benito Antonio Martínez Ocasio was born on March 10, 1994 in San Juan, Puerto Rico and grew up on the island. He studied audiovisual communications and worked ordinary jobs while uploading music to SoundCloud; his 2016 breakthrough singles and heavy streaming traction led to major-label attention. Bad Bunny's early success came from a mix of trap-inflected singles and high-profile collaborations; subsequent albums established him as a global headliner. He is noted for blending reggaeton, Latin trap and pop, for his outspoken public persona and for using fashion and performance to challenge norms.",
          "known_for": "Popularizing Latin trap and modern reggaeton globally, genre-blending production, distinctive vocal tone and a fashion-forward, outspoken public image.",
          "start_year": 2016,
          "voice_type": [
            "Baritone"
          ],
          "description": "Bad Bunny (Benito Antonio Martínez Ocasio) is a Puerto Rican singer, rapper and songwriter who helped bring Latin trap and contemporary reggaeton to a global audience. Known for genre-blending production, distinctive vocal delivery and bold fashion, he rose from SoundCloud uploads to mainstream crossover success through high-profile collaborations and multiple chart-topping albums.",
