          "biography": "Born in 1992 on the outskirts of Barcelona, Rosalía became fascinated with Spanish folk and flamenco as a teenager. She studied at the Catalonia College of Music (ESMUC), where she trained in flamenco and musicology while performing locally. Early in her career she recorded Los Ángeles with Raül Refree, a modern, stripped-back take on flamenco; she completed her studies with the baccalaureate project that evolved into El Mal Querer, produced with collaborators including El Guincho. El Mal Querer (2018) propelled her to national fame with singles such as \"Malamente\" and \"Pienso en Tu Mirá,\" earning critical acclaim and major awards. She then broadened her palette into urbano and reggaeton-influenced pop with international hits like \"Con Altura\" and continued to innovate on MOTOMAMI (2022), consolidating her global profile and award success.",
          "known_for": "Reinventing flamenco for a global pop and urbano audience through bold production, strong visuals, striking choreography and genre-blending songwriting.",
          "start_year": 2010,
          "voice_type": [
            "Mezzo-Soprano"
          ],
          "description": "Rosalía Vila Tobella (known mononymously as Rosalía) is a Spanish singer and songwriter who blends traditional flamenco with contemporary urban, pop and experimental production. Raised in Catalonia, she trained in music at the Catalonia College of Music and first gained notice with the collaborative cover album Los Ángeles (with Raül Refree) before achieving mainstream and international breakthrough with El Mal Querer, a genre-bending project that fused flamenco song forms with modern pop and hip-hop production. Since then she has explored urbano and reggaeton textures, collaborated with major global artists, and become one of Spain's most awarded and internationally recognized musical exports.",
          "instruments": [
            "Vocals"
          ],
